<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#pant-sachiv">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pant Sachiv</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sachiv</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sachiv, or Pant Sachiv, was one of the eight ministers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashta-pradhan">Ashta Pradhan</a> council created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>, responsible for royal correspondence and records. The office became hereditary in the family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shankaraji-narayan">Shankaraji Narayan</a>, appointed by Rajaram in the 1690s, and the Pant Sachivs ruled the princely state of Bhor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a> until 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pant-sachiv.jpg" alt="Pant Sachiv" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Darbar_hall,_Bhor_Palace.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
